WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.668 --> 00:00:03.480
- The first time I saw
Sadu, it was in a small shop

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.229
in the old town of Dubai.

00:00:05.229 --> 00:00:07.416
I just fell in love with these patterns.

00:00:07.416 --> 00:00:09.600
So I thought that it
would look really stunning

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.579
to take something so
Bedouin, and so heritage,

00:00:13.579 --> 00:00:15.751
and make it so modern.

00:00:15.751 --> 00:00:18.918
(gentle techno music)

00:00:29.939 --> 00:00:31.619
My name is Katya Kovtunovich.

00:00:31.619 --> 00:00:33.843
I live in Dubai, and
I'm a fashion designer.

00:00:33.843 --> 00:00:36.973
And working with Sadu is my big passion.

00:00:36.973 --> 00:00:40.563
Sadu was originally made by
Bedouin women in the desert.

00:00:40.563 --> 00:00:43.635
They would weave them
for weeks and months,

00:00:43.635 --> 00:00:47.594
but there are still amazing
artisans that make it by hand.

00:00:47.594 --> 00:00:50.293
So it's a very, very complicated art,

00:00:50.293 --> 00:00:52.955
and it's actually an art
that is disappearing.

00:00:52.955 --> 00:00:55.074
When you touch this
fabric, you really feel

00:00:55.074 --> 00:00:56.921
it's so different; it has a soul.

00:00:56.921 --> 00:00:59.421
(quiet music)

00:01:03.264 --> 00:01:06.155
I always just set myself
free and I do whatever

00:01:06.155 --> 00:01:07.635
I want with fabric.

00:01:07.635 --> 00:01:10.315
A lot of inspiration comes from traveling,

00:01:10.315 --> 00:01:13.027
from living in different
countries, living in London,

00:01:13.027 --> 00:01:16.216
observing different cultures,
and finding something

00:01:16.216 --> 00:01:18.694
that exists in one
culture and translating it

00:01:18.694 --> 00:01:21.016
into another culture.

00:01:21.016 --> 00:01:23.952
The most interesting
thing about this fabric

00:01:23.952 --> 00:01:26.475
is the stripes, that you
can take the same color,

00:01:26.475 --> 00:01:29.987
the same fabric, and
reconstruct it in so many ways.

00:01:29.987 --> 00:01:31.936
One stripe can go horizontally,

00:01:31.936 --> 00:01:35.979
one stripe can go vertically,
one stripe can go across,

00:01:35.979 --> 00:01:40.146
so you create a very different
movement on the body.

00:01:42.688 --> 00:01:44.488
Working and creating in Dubai,

00:01:44.488 --> 00:01:46.539
it's a truly unique experience.

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:50.547
Everything is coming up,
the pop art, the music,

00:01:50.547 --> 00:01:54.336
so it's just pure, calm inspiration.

00:01:54.336 --> 00:01:55.437
Nothing stops me.

00:01:55.437 --> 00:01:57.817
I can go and buy fabrics at 1:00 a.m.,

00:01:57.817 --> 00:02:01.208
I can finish my photo shoot at 3:00 a.m.

00:02:01.208 --> 00:02:04.168
You feel like anything you
desire, you can accomplish.

00:02:04.168 --> 00:02:08.636
Dubai is the city where the
word impossible doesn't exist.

00:02:08.636 --> 00:02:12.035
I think my project with
Sadu is something global.

00:02:12.035 --> 00:02:15.299
I love to see women wearing
it, and being complimented,

00:02:15.299 --> 00:02:17.058
and feeling special.

00:02:17.058 --> 00:02:21.225
And I only see a very
beautiful, interesting future.

